[narrator · hollowmere · room: The Lamplit Inn]
The Lamplit Inn. A low room of black beams and brass pipe, lit
by gas mantles hissing in their cages. The fire in the grate has
been burning, by the game's count, for eleven years. Rain and
fog press at the shutters. The floorboards are worn pale in a
path from the door to the bar, where a thousand players have
walked the same nine steps. A bookshelf by the hearth holds the
lore of the realm, which nobody reads. A notice board by the
door lists tonight's quest: THE DROWNED BELL (party of 3-5).
